1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,820
Project controls is the discipline
that turns intent into delivery.

2
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:16,780
Planning, cost, earned value, forecasting,
risk and project finance — practised as one
integrated whole, not as separate techniques.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:24,850
Project management has PMI.
Accountancy has ACCA. Finance has CFA.

4
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:30,280
Project controls has had no equivalent — no
shared standard, and no professional home.

5
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:38,280
And the discipline is changing. Schedules, forecasts
and cost reports are increasingly supported by AI.

6
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:46,040
It can accelerate analysis. It can also create false
confidence. Technology does not remove accountability.

7
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:57,070
PCI AI exists to close that gap: to give
project controls a shared standard, an
independent credential and a professional home.

8
00:00:57,070 --> 00:01:03,050
Built for how the discipline is practised
now, with AI governance at its core.

9
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:13,930
Its mission is to advance the profession through
certification, research, professional development,
standards, publications and the responsible adoption
of AI.

10
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:21,590
Its position on that adoption is
explicit. It certifies professionals
who govern AI — not who defer to it.

11
00:01:22,210 --> 00:01:30,430
The framework is the PCI AI Project
Leadership Certification Suite —
three AI-era leadership credentials.

12
00:01:31,050 --> 00:01:43,170
PCL-AI, for project controls. PFL-AI, for
project finance. PML-AI, for project management.

13
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:46,090
Finance intelligently. Control
predictively. Deliver successfully.

14
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:49,970
Each credential rests on a
published Body of Knowledge.

15
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:56,760
Its first edition defines thirteen
domains and sixty-one knowledge
areas, weighted forty, forty, twenty.

16
00:01:57,380 --> 00:02:02,110
Project accounting and finance. Project
management principles. And governed AI.

17
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:12,240
AI is not an appendix. It is a domain in its own
right, and it is embedded through the other twelve.

18
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:15,100
The examination is scenario-based
and criterion-referenced.

19
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:27,930
It asks whether you can read a cost position,
interpret an earned-value index, judge a risk
response, and decide whether an AI-generated forecast
can be trusted.

20
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:33,580
There are two routes in — an experience route
for practitioners, and a Foundation route.

21
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:42,620
The credential renews on a three-year CPD
cycle with a mandatory AI-currency component,
and every credential can be verified publicly.

22
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:53,670
The discipline is the same wherever
capital is deployed at scale, so the
credential is written to travel.

23
00:02:53,670 --> 00:03:01,220
Energy and utilities. Rail and
transportation. Aerospace and defence. Oil
and gas. Construction and infrastructure.

24
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:06,530
Aviation. Manufacturing. Data centres.
Smart cities. And government programmes.

25
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:16,290
For organisations, the same standard supports team
enrolment at scale through corporate programmes, and
curriculum alignment through university partnerships.

26
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:31,920
PCI is candid about what it is not.
It is not accredited by ANAB, IAS, or
any ISO/IEC 17024 accreditation body.

27
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:36,500
Its framework is developed with reference
to those personnel-certification
principles, and it says so plainly.

28
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:44,660
For a body whose value rests on trust, that
restraint is the foundation — not a weakness.

29
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,590
AI proposes. The professional disposes.

30
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:52,040
Discover PCI AI at pciai.org

